{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertex set is any set of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" values. The edge set is a set of unordered pairs of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{u, v}"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same edge as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{v, u}"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each slot has a row of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges; each edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop twice in its vertex’s row (as Boost stores it).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The rows share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many vertices it has. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position (open addressing with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiplicative hash, not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Dictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s SipHash) answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in O(1) expected.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-17f2v","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2o9bq","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(edge